# Which schools attack this problem, and why.
#
# This is the pairing the schools module was built for. The published solution
# leaves the graph entirely: it puts a signed matrix on the cube and reads the
# answer off an eigenvalue interlacing argument. That is a change of ground, not
# an attack on the target, so `rising-sea` is the school whose whole bet is that
# such a move exists here — and the seed names eigenvalues nowhere, so if the
# school reaches for spectra it did so from its stance rather than from recall.
#
# `chisel` is the control and must run: it will enumerate `Q_n` for small `n`,
# which is the honest thing to do and which the true solution does not need.
# The measurement is the divergence between the two, on one workspace, with the
# board carrying whatever one finds to the other.
#
# `adversarial` is left out to keep the comparison two-sided. Three schools
# share one concurrency semaphore and one budget pool, so a third is paid for
# out of the other two's attempts.
schools=chisel,rising-sea
